  "observations": [
    "A full bitstream issues LSC_INIT_ADDRESS once and streams every frame, so it never names a frame address; only a partial bitstream does.",
    "Emitted addresses are strictly descending, so ecppack walks frames in descending index order.",
    "The address space is roughly twice the frame count (max observed 19106 against 9470 frames), so the address is not a frame index.",
    "The offset (address - index) is piecewise constant with at least nine segments and is not monotonic in index: between indices 5545 and 5561 the address advances by 15 while the index advances by 16."
  ],
